Description: core: stereo3d_unpack crops each eye, and pairs a frame sequence in the stream's frames
 Crop. MLT's crop filter in a chain (Kdenlive's Crop effect) only leaves on
 the frame what it takes away (crop.left, right, top, bottom, in the samples
 of the size it was told, crop.original_width and _height, and the cropped
 size in meta.media); the producer's own crop then cuts the producer's
 picture and its resize fits what is left to the profile. As the first filter
 of a producer, stereo3d_unpack asks for the producer's picture of two views,
 so that crop cut the views as one picture, and the rescaler asked for the
 cropped size and stretched it back. Now stereo3d_unpack gives the producer's
 crop nothing to cut and asks for the producer's own size, cuts each view by
 what the crop takes (scaled from the size the crop was told to the view's own
 samples) and fits each cut view, keeping its new shape, to its half as
 filter_resize fits a picture to the profile (rint of the shapes), so a 3D
 project's eye is what a 2D project of that eye alone shows. A clip in the
 pair shape is not handed on as it is while it is cropped.
 .
 Frame sequence. The other frame of a pair was fetched at the next or the
 previous position in the profile's rate, so a sequence at twice the
 project's frame rate (a 50 fps sequence in a 25 fps project) paired frame 2p
 with frame 2p+2, the same view, and showed one eye in both. The partner
 producer now counts in the stream's own frames (a profile of its own at the
 video stream's rate, opened again at that rate because a producer counts its
 length in the rate it was opened with), and the frame's place in the stream
 is found as the avformat producer finds the frame it gives for a position.
 Which eye a frame is: the SEI's frame 0 or 1 (FFmpeg's view) or the frame's
 place in turn, exchanged by invert (H.264 D.2.26, content_interpretation_type
 2: frame 0 is the right view); before, a marked frame's eye ignored invert.
